  "inputReportSize": 20,
  "notes": "A profile outside the catalog that authors a USB device with no HID interface, function xusb, as a user's own profile may. Its descriptors are the game controller interface alone, [MS-XUSBI] 3.2.1.1, with the Microsoft OS compatible ID XUSB10. xusb_persona_check loads it to hold the authored path to its rules.",
  "layout": {
    "kind": "unspecified",
    "note": "The device has no HID interface, so no descriptor declares axes or buttons for a layout to reference. The 20-byte report's shape is in extendedReport, and SubmitState resolves its sticks and triggers canonically: X and Y, Rx and Ry, Z and Rz.",
    "source": "[MS-XUSBI] 3.2.5.1.1, Default Game Controller Input Report"
  },
  "extendedReport": {
    "reportId": "0x00",
    "size": 20,
    "alwaysArmed": true,
    "comment": "[MS-XUSBI] 3.2.5.1.1, tables 53 and 54, and GP2040-CE's XInputReport and XBOX_MASK values (headers/drivers/xinput/XInputDescriptors.h:16-49). Bit 11 of the button word is the binding switch of a wireless pad, which a wired pad never sets. The stick fields run from -32768 to 32767 with 0 at rest, and Y is inverted because the pad reports up as positive.",
